WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.507
Now we turn the prompt design into a reusable Python function.

00:00:04.507 --> 00:00:10.957
The function loops through the retrieved rows, creates a numbered source block for each one,

00:00:10.957 --> 00:00:17.392
joins those blocks into one context section, and inserts the user's question below it.

00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:22.812
Notice that the source title and source path are included with the chunk text.

00:00:22.812 --> 00:00:28.174
That gives the language model and the final answer a simple trace back to the evidence.

00:00:28.813 --> 00:00:31.235
After building the prompt, print it.

00:00:31.235 --> 00:00:35.720
Do not treat prompt construction as an invisible step.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:42.040
When an answer looks wrong, the actual prompt is one of the first things you should inspect.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.950
Check whether the correct chunks are present.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.910
Check whether the source numbering is clear.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:52.445
Check whether the instruction about insufficient evidence is included.

00:00:52.445 --> 00:00:56.956
This function gives us a consistent prompt structure for every question.
